sec.p:
The mixed algal culture was initially collected from coastal waters in proximity to Al Wakrah, Qatar. After BTEX exposure, predominant colonies were isolated through serial dilution and plating on f/2 agar. The marine algae were then grown in the BG11 medium at room temperature under a constant fluorescent light (24-h light) and intermittent CO2 injection. The pH of the growing medium was measured to be 7.4 ± 0.2, and CO2 injections were provided at consistent intervals of 5, 10, and 15 min every 48 h. Following a cultivation period of 28 days, the algae reached the exponential growth phase, which was followed by the inoculation of the algae in seawater. Algae growth rate was determined by measuring the optical density (OD) of the culture at a wavelength of 690 nm using a spectrophotometer. The dry cell weight (DCW) was calculated using Eq. (1). In addition, a calibration curve was created to establish a correlation between the biomass of the algae (measured as DCW, g/L) and the optical density measurements. The dry biomass was statistically linked to the measured optical density (OD) with a confidence level of 95%.1DrycellweightDCW=W2-W1Vg.L-1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
